module

public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Finsupp.LinearCombination
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.QuasicoherentOnSite
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Local types of modules on a ringed site

Stacks 03DL lists eight conditions on a sheaf of modules on a ringed site, each of which asks
that every object of the site have a covering on whose members the restricted module has the
corresponding global property of Stacks 03DE: being free, finite free, generated by global
sections, generated by `r` global sections, generated by finitely many global sections, having
a global presentation, having a finite global presentation, and coherence.

This file records parts (1)–(5), (7) and (8) of that definition.  Part (6), quasi-coherence, is
`SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite`, defined in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.QuasicoherentOnSite`.

## Main definitions

* `SheafOfModules.IsLocallyFreeOnSite` is part (1), local freeness.
* `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteFree` is the global finite freeness of Stacks 03DE(2).
* `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite` is part (2), finite local freeness.
* `SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite` is part (3), local generation by
  sections.
* `SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedByOnSite` is part (4), local generation by `r` sections.
* `SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalGenerators` and `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite` are
  Stacks 03DE(5) and part (5), stated categorically.
* `SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalPresentation` and
  `SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentationOnSite` are Stacks 03DE(7) and part (7), stated
  categorically.
* `SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite` is the object property cut out by the latter,
  whose full subcategory is the category of modules of finite presentation on the site.
* `PresheafOfModules.Generates` and `PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` are the sectionwise
  forms of generation by finitely many sections and of part (5).
* `PresheafOfModules.relations` is the sheaf of relations among a finite family of sections.
* `SheafOfModules.IsCoherentOnSite` is part (8), coherence.

Parts (5) and (7), finite type and finite presentation, are also Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` and `SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation`; those are registered
against Stacks 03DL here rather than redefined.

## Main results

* `SheafOfModules.isFiniteFree_iff_exists_isColimit` identifies `IsFiniteFree` with the
  direct cofan criterion when the ring and module universes agree.
* `SheafOfModules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_iff_exists_cover_isColimit` is the corresponding
  statement for `IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite`.
* `SheafOfModules.isCoherentOnSite_iff` unfolds coherence into its two conditions.
* `SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalPresentation.hasGlobalPresentation` and
  `SheafOfModules.HasFiniteGlobalPresentation.hasFiniteGlobalGenerators` compare the finite
  presentation of 03DE(7) with the two weaker global conditions, whence the instances
  `SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isFinitePresentationOnSite` and
  `SheafOfModules.isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_isFinitePresentationOnSite`.
* `SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOfGenerates` and
  `SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_presheaf_isFiniteType` connect the sectionwise finite-type
  condition to Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, so that a coherent sheaf of modules
  carries Mathlib's finite-type instance.

## Implementation notes

The conditions are stated for an arbitrary sheaf of rings `R` on an arbitrary site, not for
the structure sheaf of a bundled ringed site.  A ringed site's structure sheaf, with
commutativity forgotten, is such an `R`, so this is the more general form; it is also the form
in which `SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite` is stated.

Freeness is expressed as being a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf, specified by its
universal property, so parts (1) and (2) need no sheafification instances.  `IsFiniteFree`
compares the module with a finite free model through natural linear equivalences, which lets
the module and the ring live in independent universes; when they agree, the model can be taken
to be the module itself.  Parts (3) and (4) are phrased with Mathlib's `GeneratingSections`,
which forces the module and ring universes to agree and carries the sheafification hypotheses
needed to form the free sheaf on a slice; these are hypotheses of the existing construction,
not extra finiteness conditions.

Part (5) appears twice, in two forms that are useful for different purposes.  The categorical
form `IsFiniteTypeOnSite` uses finite coproducts and epimorphisms, so like quasi-coherence it
needs no sheafification instance.  The sectionwise form `PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` keeps
the ring and module universes independent and applies to a presheaf of modules, which is what
part (8) needs: the relations among a finite family of sections form a presheaf, and coherence
asks that this presheaf be of finite type.  Finite direct sums of copies of the structure
sheaf are finite products, so the sectionwise kernel `PresheafOfModules.relations` is the sheaf
of relations of the source.  Neither construction needs sheafification.

`HasFiniteGlobalPresentation` repeats the shape of `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` with
the index types replaced by `Fin n` and `Fin k`, and so, like it, uses universal properties only
and needs no sheafification instance.  Its module universe is independent of the universe of
the site and of the coefficient rings.  Asking for `Fin n` rather than for an arbitrary type
carrying `Finite` is no restriction — reindexing a colimiting cofan along an equivalence of
index types preserves it — and it is the shape in which the two weaker global conditions
`IsFiniteFree` and `HasFiniteGlobalGenerators` are stated here as well.

Restriction to a slice site is Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.over`, which is the restriction used
in Stacks 04IX.  A covering of an object is recorded either as a sieve generated by a family
of arrows, or as a family of objects of the slice covering its terminal object, or as a
covering sieve; the three forms are interchangeable and each is the one most convenient for
its condition.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DE)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u v w m

namespace SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

section LocallyFree

variable {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}

/-- A sheaf of modules on a site is **locally free** when every object has a covering family
on whose members the restricted module is free, that is, is a coproduct of copies of the
restricted structure sheaf.  This is Stacks 03DL(1). -/
@[stacks 03DL "locally_free", ega "0 5.4.1" "more general"]
abbrev IsLocallyFreeOnSite (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) : Prop :=
  ∀ U : C,
    ∃ (I : Type (max u v)) (V : I → C) (f : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U),
      (Sieve.ofArrows V f ∈ J U) ∧
        ∀ i : I, ∃ (B : Type w)
          (ι : ∀ _ : B, SheafOfModules.unit (R.over (V i)) ⟶ F.over (V i)),
          Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over (V i)) ι))

end LocallyFree

section FiniteLocallyFree

/-- A sheaf of modules is **finite free** when it is isomorphic to a finite coproduct of
copies of the structure sheaf.  The isomorphism is expressed by a family of linear
equivalences natural in the object of the site, so the module universe need not coincide with
the ring universe.  This is Stacks 03DE(2). -/
def IsFiniteFree (R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}) (F : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop :=
  ∃ (n : ℕ) (M : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    (ι : ∀ _ : Fin n, SheafOfModules.unit R ⟶ M),
    Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk M ι)) ∧
      ∃ e : ∀ U : Cᵒᵖ, M.val.obj U ≃ₗ[R.obj.obj U] F.val.obj U,
        ∀ {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (f : U ⟶ V) (x : M.val.obj U),
          e V (M.val.map f x) = F.val.map f (e U x)

/-- When the ring and module universes agree, the finite free model of `IsFiniteFree` can be
taken to be the module itself, which recovers the usual colimit criterion. -/
theorem isFiniteFree_iff_exists_isColimit (R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}) (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) :
    IsFiniteFree R F ↔ ∃ (n : ℕ) (ι : ∀ _ : Fin n, SheafOfModules.unit R ⟶ F),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk F ι)) := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨n, M, ι, ⟨hι⟩, e, he⟩
    let α : M ≅ F := (SheafOfModules.fullyFaithfulForget R).preimageIso
      (PresheafOfModules.isoMk (fun U => (e U).toModuleIso) (by
        intro U V f
        ext x
        exact he f x))
    exact ⟨n, fun i => ι i ≫ α.hom, ⟨hι.ofIsoColimit (Cocone.ext α fun _ ↦ rfl)⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨n, ι, hι⟩
    exact ⟨n, F, ι, hι, fun U => LinearEquiv.refl _ _, fun _ _ => rfl⟩

variable {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}

/-- A sheaf of modules on a site is **finite locally free** when every object has a covering
family on whose members the restricted module is finite free.  This is Stacks 03DL(2); rank
zero is included. -/
@[stacks 03DL "finite_locally_free", ega "0 5.4.1" "more general"]
abbrev IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite (F : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop :=
  ∀ U : C,
    ∃ (I : Type (max u v)) (V : I → C) (f : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U),
      (Sieve.ofArrows V f ∈ J U) ∧
        ∀ i : I, IsFiniteFree (R.over (V i)) (F.over (V i))

/-- The covering-family cofan criterion for finite local freeness, available when the ring and
module universes agree. -/
theorem isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite_iff_exists_cover_isColimit (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) :
    IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite F ↔
      ∀ U : C,
        ∃ (I : Type (max u v)) (V : I → C) (f : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U),
          (Sieve.ofArrows V f ∈ J U) ∧
            ∀ i : I, ∃ n : ℕ,
              ∃ (ι : ∀ _ : Fin n, SheafOfModules.unit (R.over (V i)) ⟶ F.over (V i)),
                Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk (F.over (V i)) ι)) := by
  simp only [IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite, isFiniteFree_iff_exists_isColimit]

end FiniteLocallyFree

section LocallyGenerated

variable {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}
  [∀ U : C, HasWeakSheafify (J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [∀ U : C, (J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- A sheaf of modules on a site is **locally generated by sections** when every object has a
covering on whose members the restricted module admits generating global sections.  The
covering of an object `U` is recorded as a family of objects of the slice site over `U` which
covers its terminal object.  This is Stacks 03DL(3). -/
@[stacks 03DL "locally_generated"]
abbrev IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) : Prop :=
  ∀ U : C, ∃ (I : Type (max u v)) (V : I → Over U),
    (J.over U).CoversTop V ∧
      ∀ i : I, Nonempty ((F.over (V i).left).GeneratingSections)

/-- A sheaf of modules on a site is **locally generated by `r` sections** when every object
has a covering sieve such that, for every arrow in that sieve, the restriction of the module
to its source is generated by a family of global sections indexed by a type equivalent to
`Fin r`.  This is Stacks 03DL(4). -/
@[stacks 03DL "locally_generated_r"]
abbrev IsLocallyGeneratedByOnSite (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R) (r : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ U : C, ∃ S : J.Cover U,
    ∀ (V : C) (f : V ⟶ U), S f →
      ∃ σ : (F.over V).GeneratingSections, Nonempty (σ.I ≃ Fin r)

end LocallyGenerated

section FiniteTypeOnSite

variable {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}

/-- Finitely many global sections generate a sheaf of modules when the associated map from a
finite coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf is an epimorphism.  The coproduct is
specified by its universal property, so no sheafification instance is needed.  This is Stacks
03DE(5). -/
def HasFiniteGlobalGenerators (F : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop :=
  ∃ (n : ℕ) (P : SheafOfModules.{max u v w m} R)
    (ι : ∀ _ : Fin n,
      SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, w, w, max u v m}
        (SheafOfModules.unit R) ⟶ P),
    Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι)) ∧
      ∃ π : P ⟶ SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, w, m, max u v w} F,
        Epi π

/-- A sheaf of modules on a site is **of finite type** when every object has a covering on
whose members the restricted module is generated by finitely many global sections.  This is
Stacks 03DL(5), stated with coproducts and epimorphisms instead of sheafified free sheaves, so
that it requires no sheafification instances. -/
class IsFiniteTypeOnSite (F : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop where
  /-- Finite generating families exist locally on every object. -/
  locally_finitelyGenerated : ∀ U : C,
    ∃ (I : Type (max u v)) (V : I → C) (f : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows V f ∈ J U ∧ ∀ i, HasFiniteGlobalGenerators (F.over (V i))

end FiniteTypeOnSite

section FinitePresentationOnSite

variable {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}

/-- A finite global presentation of a sheaf of modules: a cokernel of a map between *finite*
coproducts of copies of the structure sheaf.  The coproducts and the cokernel are specified by
their universal properties, so no sheafification instance is needed.

This is the finite refinement of `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation`, and the coefficient
rings and the module sections may live in different universes. -/
noncomputable def HasFiniteGlobalPresentation (F : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop :=
  ∃ (n k : ℕ) (P Q : SheafOfModules.{max u v w m} R)
    (ι : ∀ _ : Fin n, uliftForPresentation.{u, v, w, w, max u v m} (unit R) ⟶ P)
    (κ : ∀ _ : Fin k, uliftForPresentation.{u, v, w, w, max u v m} (unit R) ⟶ Q),
    Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk P ι)) ∧ Nonempty (IsColimit (Cofan.mk Q κ)) ∧
      ∃ (a : Q ⟶ P) (b : P ⟶ uliftForPresentation.{u, v, w, m, max u v w} F)
        (hab : a ≫ b = 0), Nonempty (IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ b hab))

/-- A sheaf of modules on a site is **of finite presentation** when every object of the site has
a covering on whose members the restricted module admits a finite global presentation.

This is the finite refinement of `SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite`; like it, it requires no
sheafification instance, so it also applies to the fibred categories of Stacks 06WG. -/
@[stacks 03DL "finite_presentation on an arbitrary site"]
class IsFinitePresentationOnSite (F : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop where
  /-- Finite presentations exist on a covering of each object. -/
  locally_hasFiniteGlobalPresentation : ∀ U : C,
    ∃ (I : Type (max u v)) (V : I → C) (f : ∀ i, V i ⟶ U),
      Sieve.ofArrows V f ∈ J U ∧ ∀ i, HasFiniteGlobalPresentation (F.over (V i))

namespace HasFiniteGlobalPresentation

variable {F : SheafOfModules.{m} R}

/-- A finite global presentation is a global presentation: reindex both finite coproducts by
their index types raised to the universe of the general notion. -/
theorem hasGlobalPresentation (h : HasFiniteGlobalPresentation F) :
    HasGlobalPresentation F := by
  obtain ⟨n, k, P, Q, ι, κ, ⟨hP⟩, ⟨hQ⟩, a, b, hab, hb⟩ := h
  refine ⟨ULift.{max u v w m} (Fin n), ULift.{max u v w m} (Fin k), P, Q,
    fun i ↦ ι i.down, fun i ↦ κ i.down,
    ⟨(Cofan.isColimitEquivOfEquiv Equiv.ulift (Cofan.mk P ι)) hP⟩,
    ⟨(Cofan.isColimitEquivOfEquiv Equiv.ulift (Cofan.mk Q κ)) hQ⟩, a, b, hab, hb⟩

/-- A finitely presented sheaf of modules is generated by finitely many global sections: the
presentation's cokernel projection is an epimorphism from a finite coproduct. -/
@[ega "0 5.2.5" "special case"]
theorem hasFiniteGlobalGenerators (h : HasFiniteGlobalPresentation F) :
    HasFiniteGlobalGenerators F := by
  obtain ⟨n, _, P, _, ι, _, hP, _, _, b, hab, ⟨hb⟩⟩ := h
  exact ⟨n, P, ι, hP, b, epi_of_isColimit_cofork hb⟩

end HasFiniteGlobalPresentation

/-- A sheaf of modules of finite presentation on a site is quasi-coherent. -/
@[ega "0 5.2.5" "more general"]
instance isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isFinitePresentationOnSite (F : SheafOfModules.{m} R)
    [IsFinitePresentationOnSite F] : IsQuasicoherentOnSite F where
  locally_hasGlobalPresentation U := by
    obtain ⟨I, V, f, hf, h⟩ :=
      IsFinitePresentationOnSite.locally_hasFiniteGlobalPresentation (F := F) U
    exact ⟨I, V, f, hf, fun i ↦ (h i).hasGlobalPresentation⟩

/-- A sheaf of modules of finite presentation on a site is of finite type. -/
instance isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_isFinitePresentationOnSite (F : SheafOfModules.{m} R)
    [IsFinitePresentationOnSite F] : IsFiniteTypeOnSite F where
  locally_finitelyGenerated U := by
    obtain ⟨I, V, f, hf, h⟩ :=
      IsFinitePresentationOnSite.locally_hasFiniteGlobalPresentation (F := F) U
    exact ⟨I, V, f, hf, fun i ↦ (h i).hasFiniteGlobalGenerators⟩

/-- The object property defining the category of modules of finite presentation on a site. -/
abbrev isFinitePresentationOnSite (R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}) :
    ObjectProperty (SheafOfModules.{m} R) := IsFinitePresentationOnSite

/-- An object of the full subcategory cut out by `isFinitePresentationOnSite` is of finite
presentation. -/
instance instIsFinitePresentationOnSiteFullSubcategoryObj
    (F : (isFinitePresentationOnSite R).FullSubcategory) :
    F.obj.IsFinitePresentationOnSite := F.property

end FinitePresentationOnSite

end SheafOfModules

namespace PresheafOfModules

open Opposite

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{w}}

/-- A finite family of sections of a presheaf of modules over `U` **generates** it, for a
Grothendieck topology `J`, when every section on an object over `U` is locally a linear
combination of the restrictions of the family.  This is the sheaf-theoretic meaning of
generation by global sections, written sectionwise so that the ring and module universes stay
independent. -/
def Generates (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (M : PresheafOfModules.{m} R)
    {U : C} {n : ℕ} (s : Fin n → M.obj (op U)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (V : C) (f : V ⟶ U) (t : M.obj (op V)),
    ∃ S : Sieve V, S ∈ J V ∧ ∀ (W : C) (g : W ⟶ V), S g →
      ∃ a : Fin n → R.obj (op W),
        ∑ i, a i • M.restrictₛₗ (g ≫ f).op (s i) = M.restrictₛₗ g.op t

/-- A presheaf of modules is **of finite type** for a Grothendieck topology when some family
of objects covering the site carries, on each member, a finite family of sections generating
the module.  Indexing the covering family in the universe of objects loses no generality,
since it may be indexed by the set of objects admitting generators. -/
@[sga "6 I 2.8" "special case"]
class IsFiniteType (J : GrothendieckTopology C) (M : PresheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop where
  /-- A covering family with finitely many local generators on each member. -/
  exists_generators : ∃ (I : Type u) (U : I → C), J.CoversTop U ∧
    ∀ i, ∃ (n : ℕ) (s : Fin n → M.obj (op (U i))), Generates J M s

/-- The presheaf of relations among a finite family of sections of `M` over `U`, on the slice
site over `U`.  Its value at `V ⟶ U` is the kernel of the map `R(V)^n → M(V)` sending a tuple
of coefficients to the corresponding linear combination of the restricted sections.  A finite
direct sum of copies of the structure sheaf is a finite product, so this sectionwise kernel is
the sheaf of relations of the source. -/
noncomputable def relations (M : PresheafOfModules.{m} R) {U : C} {n : ℕ}
    (s : Fin n → M.obj (op U)) :
    PresheafOfModules.{w} ((Over.forget U).op ⋙ R) where
  obj V := ModuleCat.of _ (LinearMap.ker
    (Fintype.linearCombination (R.obj (op V.unop.left))
      (fun i ↦ M.restrictₛₗ V.unop.hom.op (s i))))
  map {V W} f := ModuleCat.ofHom
    (Y := (ModuleCat.restrictScalars (R.map f.unop.left.op).hom).obj
      (ModuleCat.of _ (LinearMap.ker
        (Fintype.linearCombination (R.obj (op W.unop.left))
          (fun i ↦ M.restrictₛₗ W.unop.hom.op (s i))))))
    { toFun := fun a ↦ ⟨fun i ↦ R.map f.unop.left.op (a.val i), by
        have h := congrArg (M.restrictₛₗ f.unop.left.op) a.property
        change (∑ i, R.map f.unop.left.op (a.val i) •
          M.restrictₛₗ W.unop.hom.op (s i)) = 0
        change M.restrictₛₗ f.unop.left.op
          (∑ i, a.val i • M.restrictₛₗ V.unop.hom.op (s i)) =
            M.restrictₛₗ f.unop.left.op 0 at h
        have hc (i : Fin n) :
            M.restrictₛₗ f.unop.left.op (M.restrictₛₗ V.unop.hom.op (s i)) =
              M.restrictₛₗ W.unop.hom.op (s i) :=
          (M.map_comp_apply _ _ _).symm.trans
            (M.congr_map_apply (congrArg Quiver.Hom.op (Over.w f.unop)) _)
        simpa only [map_sum, map_smulₛₗ, hc, map_zero] using h⟩
      map_add' := by
        intro a b
        apply Subtype.ext
        funext i
        exact map_add _ _ _
      map_smul' := by
        intro r a
        apply Subtype.ext
        funext i
        exact map_mul _ _ _ }
  map_id V := by
    apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
    apply LinearMap.ext
    intro a
    apply Subtype.ext
    funext i
    exact congrArg (fun f ↦ f (a.val i)) (R.map_id _)
  map_comp f g := by
    apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
    apply LinearMap.ext
    intro a
    apply Subtype.ext
    funext i
    exact congrArg (fun f ↦ f (a.val i)) (R.map_comp f.unop.left.op g.unop.left.op)

end PresheafOfModules

namespace SheafOfModules

open Opposite

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}

/-- A sheaf of modules on a site is **coherent** when it is of finite type and, for every
object `U` and every finite family of sections over `U`, the sheaf of relations among that
family is of finite type on the slice site over `U`.  This is Stacks 03DL(8). -/
@[stacks 03DL "coherent", ega "0 5.3.7"]
class IsCoherentOnSite (F : SheafOfModules.{m} R) : Prop where
  /-- A coherent sheaf of modules is of finite type. -/
  isFiniteType : PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType J F.val
  /-- Every finite family of sections has a finite-type sheaf of relations. -/
  kernel_isFiniteType : ∀ (U : C) (n : ℕ) (s : Fin n → F.val.obj (op U)),
    PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType (J.over U) (PresheafOfModules.relations F.val s)

attribute [instance] IsCoherentOnSite.isFiniteType

/-- Coherence is finite type together with finite type of the sheaf of relations of every
finite family of sections on every slice site. -/
theorem isCoherentOnSite_iff (F : SheafOfModules.{m} R) :
    IsCoherentOnSite F ↔ PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType J F.val ∧
      ∀ (U : C) (n : ℕ) (s : Fin n → F.val.obj (op U)),
        PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType (J.over U) (PresheafOfModules.relations F.val s) :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨h.isFiniteType, h.kernel_isFiniteType⟩, fun ⟨hft, hker⟩ ↦ ⟨hft, hker⟩⟩

/-- A section of a sheaf of modules over `U` is a global section of its restriction to the
slice site over `U`. -/
noncomputable def sectionOver (M : SheafOfModules.{m} R) {U : C} (s : M.val.obj (op U)) :
    (M.over U).sections :=
  PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk (fun V ↦ M.val.map V.unop.hom.op s) (by
    intro V W f
    change M.val.map f.unop.left.op (M.val.map V.unop.hom.op s) = _
    rw [← M.val.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp, Over.w f.unop])

/-- A finite family of sections generating a sheaf of modules over `U`, in the sectionwise
sense of `PresheafOfModules.Generates`, gives Mathlib's generating sections of the restriction
to the slice site over `U`: the associated map from the free sheaf is locally surjective,
hence an epimorphism. -/
noncomputable def generatingSectionsOfGenerates
    (M : SheafOfModules.{w} R) {U : C} {n : ℕ} (s : Fin n → M.val.obj (op U))
    (hs : PresheafOfModules.Generates J M.val s)
    [HasWeakSheafify (J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [(J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] :
    (M.over U).GeneratingSections where
  I := ULift.{w} (Fin n)
  s i := sectionOver M (s i.down)
  epi := by
    let p := (M.over U).freeHomEquiv.symm (fun i : ULift.{w} (Fin n) ↦
      sectionOver M (s i.down))
    change Epi p
    have hp (V : (Over U)ᵒᵖ) (i : Fin n) :
        p.val.app V ((SheafOfModules.freeSection (R := R.over U) (ULift.up i)).val V) =
          M.val.map V.unop.hom.op (s i) :=
      congrArg (fun t : (M.over U).sections ↦ t.val V)
        (SheafOfModules.sectionsMap_freeHomEquiv_symm_freeSection
          (fun i : ULift.{w} (Fin n) ↦ sectionOver M (s i.down)) (ULift.up i))
    have : PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective (J.over U) p.val := by
      constructor
      intro V t
      obtain ⟨T, hT, ht⟩ := hs V.left V.hom t
      apply (J.over U).superset_covering _ (J.overEquiv_symm_mem_over V T hT)
      intro W f hf
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := ht W.left f.left hf
      let a' : Fin n → (R.over U).obj.obj (op W) := fun i ↦ a i
      let t' : (SheafOfModules.free (R := R.over U) (ULift.{w} (Fin n))).val.obj (op W) :=
        ∑ i : Fin n, a' i •
          (SheafOfModules.freeSection (R := R.over U) (ULift.up i)).eval (op W)
      refine ⟨t', ?_⟩
      change (p.val.app (op W)).hom
        (∑ i : Fin n, a' i •
          (SheafOfModules.freeSection (R := R.over U) (ULift.up i)).eval (op W)) =
        M.val.restrictₛₗ f.left.op t
      rw [map_sum]
      simp only [map_smul]
      change (∑ i : Fin n, a' i •
        p.val.app (op W) ((SheafOfModules.freeSection (R := R.over U)
          (ULift.up i)).val (op W))) = _
      simp only [hp]
      have hh (i : Fin n) : M.val.restrictₛₗ (f.left ≫ V.hom).op (s i) =
          M.val.map W.hom.op (s i) :=
        M.val.congr_map_apply (congrArg Quiver.Hom.op (Over.w f)) _
      simp only [hh] at ha
      exact ha
    have : (SheafOfModules.toSheaf (R.over U)).ReflectsEpimorphisms :=
      Functor.reflectsEpimorphisms_of_faithful _
    apply (SheafOfModules.toSheaf (R.over U)).epi_of_epi_map
    have : Sheaf.IsLocallySurjective ((SheafOfModules.toSheaf (R.over U)).map p) :=
      ‹PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective (J.over U) p.val›
    exact Sheaf.epi_of_isLocallySurjective _

/-- The sectionwise finite-type condition on the underlying presheaf of modules supplies
Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` instance whenever the ring and module universes
coincide. -/
theorem isFiniteType_of_presheaf_isFiniteType (M : SheafOfModules.{w} R)
    (h : PresheafOfModules.IsFiniteType J M.val)
    [∀ U : C, HasWeakSheafify (J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : C, (J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] :
    M.IsFiniteType := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨I, U, hU, hgen⟩ := h.exists_generators
  choose n s hs using hgen
  let q : M.LocalGeneratorsData :=
    { I := I
      X := U
      coversTop := hU
      generators i := generatingSectionsOfGenerates M (s i) (hs i) }
  exact ⟨⟨q, ⟨fun i ↦ ⟨inferInstanceAs (Finite (ULift.{w} (Fin (n i))))⟩⟩⟩⟩

/-- A coherent sheaf of modules supplies Mathlib's finite-type instance when its ring and
module universes coincide. -/
instance isFiniteType_of_isCoherentOnSite
    [∀ U : C, HasWeakSheafify (J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [∀ U : C, (J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    (M : SheafOfModules.{w} R) [IsCoherentOnSite M] : M.IsFiniteType :=
  isFiniteType_of_presheaf_isFiniteType M (IsCoherentOnSite.isFiniteType (R := R))

end SheafOfModules

